      en: "Barysaw, situated northeast of Minsk along the banks of the Berezina River, is a city steeped in dramatic history while maintaining a strong modern industrial presence. The city is globally recognized for the Battle of Berezina in 1812, where Napoleon's retreating Grande Armée suffered catastrophic losses during a harrowing river crossing; several monuments in the area commemorate this turning point in European history. In the contemporary era, Barysaw has gained international recognition through sports, largely due to the success of BATE Borisov, a football club that has frequently competed in the UEFA Champions League. The team's home, the futuristic Borisov Arena, stands as a striking piece of modern architecture. Economically, Barysaw thrives on heavy machinery production, pharmaceuticals, and extensive wood processing industries."
